"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"text":" that emits the same elements as the upstream but retries on failure using the given strategy,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"performing the transformation before each retry.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The provided transformation closure is executed ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" each retry, allowing for side effects such as refreshing tokens or resetting state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The closure’s returned ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always fully consumed before the retry occurs, but its elements are ignored.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The element type of the returned sequence does not need to match the upstream’s element type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful for performing asynchronous side effects like credential refresh before retrying the main sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example: Refreshing an access token on a 401 HTTP error before retrying the main request","type":"heading","anchor":"Example-Refreshing-an-access-token-on-a-401-HTTP-error-before-retrying-the-main-request"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let mainRequest = URLSession.shared.dataTaskAsyncSequence(for: URLRequest(url: URL(string: \"https:\/\/api.example.com\/data\")!))","","let retriedSequence = mainRequest.retry(.byCount(3)) { error in","    \/\/ If error is 401 Unauthorized, refresh token before retrying","    DeferredTask {","        if let urlError = error as? URLError, urlError.code == .userAuthenticationRequired {","     